Section: Setting up the radio
  The sim reads a radio that is in USB joystick mode as a game controller. The first time, it has
  to learn which stick is which, and which buttons you gave to the autopilot. This is the
  calibration. The sim saves it in the file controls.cfg, and the next start uses it. This
  section uses the RadioMaster TX15 with EdgeTX. Another EdgeTX radio works the same way.

Background:
  Given the radio is not calibrated
